{
  "bug_id": "GH-18902",
  "title": "OpenSSL backend skips requested OCSP verification on TLS session resumption",
  "severity": "potential_revocation_check_bypass_pending_replay",
  "keywords": [
    "TLS",
    "OCSP",
    "session resumption",
    "certificate status"
  ],
  "product": "curl",
  "component": "libcurl OpenSSL TLS backend",
  "creation_time": "2025-10-07",
  "resolution_time": "2025-10-07T23:56:25+02:00",
  "bug_discussion": "Public fixing PR: https://github.com/curl/curl/pull/18902\nThe upstream reporter states that resumed TLS sessions skip OCSP stapled-response verification and proposes forcing a full handshake when CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYSTATUS is enabled.\n\nPrior reporter issue: https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/12399\nIts public C program performs two requests on one easy handle, sets CURLOPT_SSL_VERIFYSTATUS and CURLOPT_FORBID_REUSE, and observes TLS session reuse on the second request. The original 2023 report asked that OCSP verification be skipped on resumed sessions because those sessions carry no new stapled response. That behavior was introduced by the mainline change associated with https://github.com/curl/curl/pull/12418. The 2025 fix adopts a stricter check by disabling resumption for this option.",
  "commit_ids": [
    "4bfd7a961521e1fd6aab7610e931d82a342781a8"
  ],
  "fix_commit_sha": "4bfd7a961521e1fd6aab7610e931d82a342781a8",
  "fix_date": "2025-10-07T23:56:25+02:00",
  "season": "2025H2",
  "mainline_verified": true,
  "date_basis": "git_committer_date_on_captured_origin_master",
  "affected_files": [
    "lib/vtls/openssl.c"
  ],
  "changed_lines": 3,
  "aliases": [
    "PR-18902"
  ],
  "target_type": "libcurl_openssl_tls_session_resumption",
  "report_references": [
    {
      "id": "GH-18902",
      "url": "https://github.com/curl/curl/pull/18902",
